  {
    "id": "ded2d12c17c32a8f4984",
    "source": "Keep the party's location current: whenever a scene opens somewhere new or the party moves to a different area, call move_party with the area's name and a concrete layout description before narrating. The call belongs in the reply whose narration has them arrive, whatever else that reply does: narrating a roll that got them there (a climb, a forced door, a found path), a stretch of travel (travel covers the distance, never the place), or a question to the players. Going back to an area they left is a move too: give move_party the name GAME STATE already lists for it and leave out the layout, which the server keeps. Use update_location when they learn more about the current area. GAME STATE's location block must always match the fiction.",
    "sourceHash": "ded2d12c17c32a8f4984fea81a3d907c346bbff63d80b1a406a65a60274fd52d",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/lib/dm/prompt-rules.ts",
        "line": 146,
        "property": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
